This Python function calculates the product of all positive numbers and the sum of absolute values of all negative numbers in an array. If there are no negative numbers, it returns -1 raised to the power of the length of the array. Otherwise, it multiplies the product of positive numbers by the sum of absolute values of negative numbers.

=== code written from the explanation ===

