This Python function takes a string as input and replaces sequences of three or more spaces with a hyphen followed by the space character, and sequences of two or more spaces with an underscore followed by the space character. It iterates through each character in the input string, tracking the start and end indices of consecutive spaces. When it encounters a non-space character, it checks the length of the sequence of spaces and appends the appropriate replacement to the output string. Finally, it handles any remaining spaces that were not part of a sequence.

