This Python function takes two planet names as input and returns a tuple containing the names of all planets located between them in our solar system, sorted alphabetically. It first checks if both inputs are valid planet names and if they are not the same. If so, it finds the indices of these planets in the list of all planets. Based on their order, it slices the list to get the planets between them and returns them as a tuple.

